.el .ds Aq '
.TH dfdu-recover 1  "dfdu-recover " 
.SH NAME
dfdu\-recover \- List what earlier sessions left unfinished (staged items, interrupted deletes), and finish, restore or dismiss them
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdfdu recover\fR [\fB\-\-finish\fR] [\fB\-\-restore\fR] [\fB\-\-dismiss\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
List what earlier sessions left unfinished (staged items, interrupted deletes), and finish, restore or dismiss them
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-finish\fR \fI<N>\fR
Delete what is left of these staged items (numbers from the list)
.TP
\fB\-\-restore\fR \fI<N>\fR
Put these staged items back at their paths (next to them as NAME.restored\-N if something is there now), or take these items found in the trash back out of it
.TP
\fB\-\-dismiss\fR \fI<N>\fR
Close these interrupted items: nothing is done on disk
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Finish and restore. Without it nothing is changed: what would be done is printed
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
